WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.285
Ask a chat AI to turn your
rough notes into an email,

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:06.723
and it does a tidy job in seconds.

00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:09.859
Ask it which regional rule
covers your stock water,

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:12.574
and it might invent one.

00:00:13.024 --> 00:00:16.068
Both answers will sound
just as sure of themselves.

00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:19.133
So it pays to know which
jobs it's good at.

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:20.875
It's good at drafting.

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:24.217
Emails, notices, a job ad for a farm hand.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:29.894
It's good at summing up a long document,
explaining a term in plain words,

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:33.865
and giving you a list of
options to think about.

00:00:34.315 --> 00:00:36.396
These jobs have something in common.

00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:39.090
You can check the result
yourself, quickly,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.163
because you know the farm and
you know what you meant to say.

00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:44.975
Now, what it gets wrong.

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:46.726
First, it makes things up.

00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:49.071
Remember, it picks likely words.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:50.894
Ask about a rule,

00:00:51.148 --> 00:00:53.311
and it can write a rule that sounds real,

00:00:53.331 --> 00:00:56.316
with a name, a year and a number.

00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:59.740
There's no 2024 Stock Water Rule.

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:01.982
We made that one up to show you.

00:01:02.002 --> 00:01:05.779
It has a year, a number and
an official-sounding name,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:08.354
and none of it is real.

00:01:08.804 --> 00:01:11.221
Second, its knowledge can be out of date.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:16.226
It only knows text up to a certain
date, so recent changes to rules,

00:01:16.246 --> 00:01:19.557
prices or schemes might be missing.

00:01:20.007 --> 00:01:22.702
Third, it doesn't know your farm.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.779
Your soils, your stock, your history.

00:01:25.812 --> 00:01:30.063
Unless you tell it, it's
guessing from farms in general.

00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:34.404
The hard part is that you can't
tell a wrong answer from its tone.

00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:36.320
A made-up fact

00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:39.779
reads just as smoothly as a true one.

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:42.286
So when it matters, check.

00:01:42.632 --> 00:01:45.641
Ask for a source you can
open and read yourself.

00:01:45.895 --> 00:01:48.475
Make sure any numbers
match your own records.

00:01:48.495 --> 00:01:53.118
And ask the question a different
way, to see if the answer holds.

00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:57.449
For anything about rules,
money, animal health or safety,

00:01:57.469 --> 00:01:59.340
check with the people who'd know.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:03.438
Your council, your vet, your accountant.

00:02:03.888 --> 00:02:08.464
Below the video, try spotting the
made-up fact in a few real answers.
